{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"] "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s (34 n from 5,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Traps when the work limit is spent: 4,000 + 20√n products on σI − L (then shift-invert),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000 shift-invert products, 20,000 + 2n per solve. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached it in the measurements.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectralordering(weight:normalized:tolerance:)-197t5"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:)-197t5"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spectral ordering (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spectral_ordering"},{"type":"text","text":"; Barnard, Pothen and Simon): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components in order of their least vertex index; a component of at most two vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order; a larger one ascending by the Fiedler vector of that component (for a connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fiedlerVector()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s), entries within 10⁻⁸ · max|x| of their predecessor kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"type":"text","text":" for the empty graph."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE16spectralOrdering6weight10normalized9toleranceSay6VertexQzGqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SbSdtSBRd__lF","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralOrdering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind